                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I kickstarted this game on the strength of the art, and on that front it delivered.  It sports gorgeous water-color styled illustrations and animated backgrounds, and some interesting character design inspired by Japanese folklore.\n\nIt's the writing that disappointed me.  The story itself is fine, but the writing style is awkward and circuitous.  I am all for creative writers taking license with language, but the grammar used in the English text was often ungainly and made the story feel tedious.  I can't comment on the Russian text, but the English version would benefit greatly from a skilled editor.\n\nThe game is also very short--Steam tells me it took 0.9 hours to finish the entire game, with multiple endings, minus some of the extras that I didn't finish.  The overall leagth is not as much the issue as the lack of choice, for me.  Almost none of the choices in the game are far-reaching.  [spoiler]There's a part where the main character is being tested in certain ways, and instead of giving the player choices and putting the onus on us to pass these tests, that part is entirely kinetic, ie no choices.  The game neglects a good opportunity to get the player more invested in the story by forcing us to address moral dilemmas in the character's shoes.[/spoiler]\n\nTL;DR it's really pretty but very short and not fantastically written.",
